The task is to predict whether a passenger was transported to an alternate dimension during the Spaceship Titanic's collision with the spacetime anomaly. (lines 1-2)

The dataset is a set of personal records recovered from the ship's damaged computer system, which includes two files: `train.csv` and `test.csv`. (lines 3-4)

The task is to predict the value of `Transported` for the passengers in the `test.csv` file, based on the information provided in the `train.csv` file. (lines 5-6)

The `train.csv` file contains the following information:

* `PassengerId`: a unique Id for each passenger (lines 7-8)
* `HomePlanet`: the planet the passenger departed from (lines 9-10)
* `CryoSleep`: whether the passenger elected to be put into suspended animation for the duration of the voyage (lines 11-12)
* `Cabin`: the cabin number where the passenger is staying (lines 13-14)
* `Destination`: the planet the passenger will be debarking to (lines 15-16)
* `Age`: the age of the passenger (lines 17-18)
* `VIP`: whether the passenger has paid for special VIP service during the voyage (lines 19-20)
* `RoomService`, `FoodCourt`, `ShoppingMall`, `Spa`, `VRDeck`: the amount the passenger has billed at each of the Spaceship Titanic's many luxury amenities (lines 21-22)

The `test.csv` file contains the same information as the `train.csv` file, except for the `Transported` column, which is the target to be predicted. (lines 23-24)

The `sample_submission.csv` file contains the predicted values for the `Transported` column for the passengers in the `test.csv` file. (lines 25-26)
